{"name":"Baked Apple","hex":"#b34646","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baked-apple","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of bakeapple (“the cloudberry”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baked-apple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baked apple","blocks":[{"text":"A baked apple is a dish consisting of an apple baked in an oven, until it becomes soft. The core is usually removed and the resulting cavity is stuffed with sweet or savory fillings and seasonings. Pears and quinces may be prepared in the same way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Hot_and_Sweet_Baked_Apples_-_50495578482.jpg/330px-Hot_and_Sweet_Baked_Apples_-_50495578482.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baked_apple","wikidata":"Q3441161"},{"title":"Baking","blocks":[{"text":"Baking is a method of preparing food that uses dry heat, typically in an oven, hot ashes, or on hot stones. The most commonly baked foods in 2025 were bread and rolls. Heat is gradually transferred from the surface of unbaked goods to their center, typically at elevated temperatures surpassing 300 °F. Dry heat cooking imparts a distinctive richness to foods through the processes of caramelization and surface browning. As heat travels through, it transforms batters and doughs into baked goods and more with a firm dry crust and a softer center. Baking can be combined with grilling to produce a hybrid barbecue variant by using both methods simultaneously, or one after the other. Baking is related to barbecuing because the concept of the masonry oven is similar to that of a smoke pit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg/330px-Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baking","wikidata":"Q720398"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Brat%C3%A4pfel_1.JPG/500px-Brat%C3%A4pfel_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Brat%C3%A4pfel_1.JPG/1280px-Brat%C3%A4pfel_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Brat%C3%A4pfel_1.JPG/500px-Brat%C3%A4pfel_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bratäpfel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrat%C3%A4pfel_1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg/500px-Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg/1280px-Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org